
Project Name- Command-Line Word & Character Counter + JSON Logger
Command-Line Word & Character Counter + JSON Logger

What it does?
 It reads a sentence or a text file, counts words, characters, and vowels, and logs past analyses into a local JSON or text file so you can review your history.

Thing I learnt building it:


What You Will Learn

• Input/Output (input(), file handling): Reading user input or loading a .txt file.
• Strings & Methods: Using .lower(), .strip(), and character iteration.
• Data Structures (Dictionaries & Lists): Storing frequency counts or session logs.
• Control Flow & Loops: while loops for a menu system.
• JSON Serialization (json module): Saving and loading data from disk.
• Functions & Scope: Organizing code into clean, reusable blocks.
